  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the man in the suit",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the man in a suit sitting at a desk, as the meme implies that this person (the man) is the entity attempting the absurd action described in the text. The humor and satire derive from the user identifying with or imagining themselves as the person being mocked — the bureaucrat or official who is so incompetent that they would send killers to kill Dante in his own Inferno. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you' in the text, but the satirical framing inherently invites the user to project themselves onto the figure of authority depicted.",
